Z||000000||fiero56||05-20-2000||11:28 PM||||I have an '88 with the light grey interior. The overhead light on mine has two switches controlling the lights on each side, and the dome light is in the center with no switch. I am wondering if there were any light grey fixtures like this made with three buttons(one on each side and one in the middle). If so, does anyone have one they are willing to part with, for a price?||||reg||1
Z||000001||BroCar 87||05-21-2000||01:37 AM||||Hey Fiero56, I don't believe they made one with three because they middle two lights are used as courtesy lights. They are made to come on as the door opens or the dimmer switch is activated. The outside two are the only ones that are activated by the buttons.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ed||05-21-2000||01:42 AM||||If it wasn't clear, the center lights can be turned on by the dash light wheel being  run all the way up.||||reg||1
Z||000003||BN Boomer||05-21-2000||03:19 AM||||My 85 GT, saddle interior, has the light housing with 3 buttons. The outside 2 operate the corresponding map/reading lamps and the center one operates the center lamp (wow, go figure!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ). Rotating the dimmer wheel all the way up turns on both the center lamp as well as the underdash courtesy lamps.||||reg||4
